    "name": "text",
    "text": "<p>In this module, we saw:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Examples of classes that contain fields of the types of other classes we wrote – <em>nested data</em>.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Using <strong>wish lists</strong> to keep track of methods we should implement next, in order to break down a larger problem.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>Examples of <code>double</code>s, which can represent fractional numbers, but only approximately.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>The built-in module <code>Math</code> (see the documentation <a href=\"https://docs.oracle.com/javase/9/docs/api/java/lang/Math.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\">here</a>), which has methods that we can call to perform calculations such as square root.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>",
